        <p>THE PRICE OF BREAD.</p>
        <p>REMARKABLE CHEAPNESS OF FLOUR.</p>
        <p>In consequence of the low price of bread and flour at the Spalding Workhouse (21d. per 41b. loaf and Is. stone flour, or whole meal 83. a stone), a proposal has been brought before the guardians to fez,d the pigs at the Unionhouse on the contract wheat meal, instead of the usual pie food, which costs more, and this proposal , has been referred to a committee. In consequence of the report of the low price, there has been a large number of inquiries, and samples of the bread, which has been pronounced good, have been solicited. It has been cited as a proof of extravagnnt charges made by bakers in London and eleswhere for bread. The Spalding bakers declare that it is impossible to supply the bread at the price, but the contractor states that it allows him a mita profit at the contract prices quoted.</p>
