      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-01-14_WidnesExaminer_art0104" n="art0104">
        <head>WARRINGTON MUSEUM</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON MUSEUM</p>
        <p>The following are some of the additions to the Library during the last three months : Ritchie's " Records of Tennyson, Browning, and Ruskin," Hutton's "Cardinal Manning, " Besant's "London," Stevensona " Footnote to history," Wood- ford's "Naturalist among the head-hunters," Duffy's "Tuscan republics," " Missing friends," 66 Blockade runners" (Adventure series), Well's "Oxford and Oxford life,' Billing's " Scientific materialism," Wise's " Industrial freedom," Stanton's" Place of authority in religious belief," Muirhead's " Elements of Ethics," Mayeux's "Decorative composition," Cotterill's " Ap- plied mechanics," Thomson's " Study of animal life," Whiall and Denny's "Cockroach," Roscoe and Schorlemmer's "Inorganic chemistry, 2v . Wyatt's "Manual of continuation schools, Wright's "Man and the glacial period," Lubbock's "Beauties of nature," Sutherland's" Manual of commercial instruc- tion," "Coins and medals," edited by Lane-Poole, Woodward's " Geology of England and Wales," Page's 6` Advanced geology,' Hellyer s "Plumbing," Fisher's "Elementary chemistry," Gallon's "Healthy dwel- lings," Gray's " Electrical influence machines,' " Can- tor lectures," 18 vols., Muir's "Principles of , chemistry," " Coursing and falconry," (Badminton), Cassell's ' New popular educator,Bv." Furniss's " Flying visits," Huxley's "Essays on controverted questions," Brandon's'6 Analysis of Gothic architecture," Blanche's Extravaganzas," Barkley's " Art of rat-catching," " The argosy, 34v.," Twain's " American claimant," Flertzka's "Freeland," Lang's " Green fairy book," Molesworth's " In an enchanted garden," Hardy's " Group of noble dames," and " Tess of the D'urbervilles," Olipbant's "Railway man and his children," Farrar's " Darkness and dawn," Stevenson's " The wrecker," Corelli's " Thelma," Betant's " Dorothy Wallis," Du Manner's 6' Peter Ibbetson," Lawless's " Grania," Linskill's " Cleveden," Zola's "The downfall, " The new Anti- gone." Music :—" Mantana," " Ivanhoe," "Carmen,' " Ernani," " Fidelis," and novels by Winter, Marryatt, St. Aultyn, Clarke Russell, Alexander (2), Fenn, Praed, Whitley, Dora Russell, Wilson (3), Barr, Argles (5), Carey (2), Crawford (3), Caine, Doyle, F. M. Robinson.</p>
