        <p>" THOOSE TAWL HATS I" --- " Mary, wot art dooin' theer ? Fotchin' eaut my Sunday hat? Doesn't know that th' very Beet on't Puts me into a cowd swat? Ever sin' we startet coortin', Aw've inform'd thee, plump an' flat, Aw'm noan beaun' to smirk an' swagger, Wi' a chimbley-mowlded hat It's aw reet fer "Jock free Paisley," Wearin' urn to cut a dash ; Caunt theau see, my lass, his market's Not made yet, so he mun mash? But aw'm thiukin' a Glengairy Wud just suit him up to th' hilt, If he'd only drop his treausers, An' cum eaut i' dirk an' kilt I An' it's maybe—wot &amp;et caw it?— Quite professional fer "Fred," To be allus, wen i' bizness, Wi' a stovepipe on his yed. Wot theau thinks on't's rayther deaubtful, But fer me it's straight an' clear, He'd look nicer in a turban, Wi' a tossle o'er his earl Ez fer" William," oft aw've heerd him, Wen he's put his shiner on, Bless thoose vile abominations, Heartily, an' like a moo ! An' aw've railly heerd him punnin', Even wen he's in a pelt; Fer he's cawd ther silken" darkness, Summut moor then cud be felt !" Ther's no deaubt theere th' wost inventions Ever plann'd for men an' lads: An' like wimmin's poncake toppin's, Made fer't tickle fashion's fads. Wy, suppose theau guz to th' Theeter, An' gets in a feight er crush. Its" a hundert to a hay seed," That a guinea's .woth guz smush ! Well, then, Mary, thee tak' warnin', If theau will upset my views, Ther'll be inklin's ov a inquest, Comin' want i'th' " Evening News." Fer ez lung ez aw con waddle To my wark on these owd legs, Aw'll nare wear 'um—aw'll be d.—d fost I An' aw've sworn it— THU 0' PEGS. Rose Bonk, January 12, 1893.</p>
