        <p>LATEST NE WS. SIR. ANDREW WALKER. Yesterday morning the bulletin from Gateacre was to , the effect that there was no change in the condition of Sir Andrew Walker. DEATH OF A LEIGH FOOTBALLER. Yesterday morning, at half-past nine, Isaac Taylor, aged twenty-four, of Henrietta-st., Leigh, one of the Leigh forwards, died from inflammation of the lungs, after a week's illness. On October 29, whilst playing for Leigh azainst Kendal Hornets, he had his jaw broken, but this in no way, from a medical opinion, con- tributed towards his death. He was very well respected in Lancashire. IHE HOME RULE BILL. --- MR. GLADSTONE AND MR. JUSTIN WCARTHY. Mr. Gladstone, Mr. John Morley, and Mr. Justin M‘Carthv had a conference yesterday morning at Downing-street, regarding the Home Rule Bill. In view of the Cabinet Council, which is to be held in the after- noon, this conference is considered to be one of great importance. The interview lasted nearly half an hour. Mr. M`Carthy left before Mr. Morley, who remained with the Premier some time longer. A Cabinet Council was afterwards held and was attended by all the Ministers.</p>
